WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit
8: Numbers, Shapes, and Measurement.

2
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.754
In this unit you use English to talk about maths in real life.

3
00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:14.409
You count and name big numbers, all the way up to one million.

4
00:00:14.489 --> 00:00:19.739
You learn the words addition,
subtraction, multiplication and division.

5
00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:27.997
You measure the size, height, weight and distance of
things around you, using words like metre and centimetre.

6
00:00:28.077 --> 00:00:32.201
You also hunt for straight lines and repeating patterns.

7
00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:37.906
Maths is everywhere: in the market, in
the kitchen and on the way to school.

8
00:00:37.986 --> 00:00:44.738
By the end you will solve a number puzzle,
just like Amal and Sami do in this unit's story.

9
00:00:44.818 --> 00:00:51.044
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:51.124 --> 00:00:57.998
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
read and say big numbers, up to one million.

11
00:00:58.078 --> 00:01:04.639
You will also use the maths words addition,
subtraction, multiplication and division.

12
00:01:04.719 --> 00:01:10.968
You will also measure the size, height,
weight and distance of things around you.

13
00:01:11.048 --> 00:01:13.859
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:20.151
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
number, million, fact, pattern, straight, addition.

15
00:01:20.231 --> 00:01:25.405
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:29.492
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:29.572 --> 00:01:33.791
The reading sequence includes Maths
Is Everywhere and A Pattern Poem.

18
00:01:33.871 --> 00:01:34.663
Read actively.

19
00:01:34.743 --> 00:01:38.963
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:39.043 --> 00:01:43.012
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:43.092 --> 00:01:47.097
The first language focus is Present Simple and Imperatives.

22
00:01:47.177 --> 00:01:55.405
The Present Simple tells about things that happen often or
facts that are always true, like “The sun rises in the east.”

23
00:01:55.485 --> 00:02:00.182
An imperative is a command or
instruction, like “Measure the height.”

24
00:02:00.262 --> 00:02:04.197
Both help us speak and write clearly, especially in maths.

25
00:02:04.277 --> 00:02:11.743
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

26
00:02:11.823 --> 00:02:15.965
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Measure and Tell.

27
00:02:16.045 --> 00:02:20.601
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

28
00:02:20.681 --> 00:02:24.131
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

29
00:02:24.211 --> 00:02:27.798
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

30
00:02:27.878 --> 00:02:29.458
You are ready to begin.

31
00:02:29.538 --> 00:02:36.603
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

32
00:02:36.683 --> 00:02:40.068
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

33
00:02:40.148 --> 00:02:48.079
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
